      "sha": "59e141d3300a263369ce6f0431a42f7ca33e3b97",
      "message": "feat(wordcount): add @floatboat/nexus-plugin-wordcount with markdown-aware stats\n\nIntroduces a new workspace package that layers a markdown-aware\nword / character / CJK / reading-time counter on top of the editor's\nexisting AST. Closes the gap between the naive\nEditorAPI.getDocumentStats() (which counts markdown syntax and treats\na 1000-character Chinese note as a single 'word') and what\nnotes-app hosts actually want to display.\n\nPublic surface (packages/plugin-wordcount):\n\n- countMarkdown(source, options) — pure function, walks mdast,\n  excludes code / math / HTML / frontmatter / definitions by default,\n  CJK-aware word counting, dual-rate reading time (Latin wpm + CJK cpm)\n- createWordCountPlugin(options) — returns a NexusPlugin + query\n  handle. Subscribes to editor change / selectionChange events;\n  full-doc recompute is debounced (default 150ms), selection\n  recompute is synchronous. Reuses editor.getAst() so there is no\n  double parsing on the hot path.\n- createStatusBar(plugin, options) — vanilla-DOM, role=status +\n  aria-live=polite, framework-agnostic, fully i18n-able.\n- attachWordCountPlugin(plugin, editor) — ergonomic binder.\n\nWired into apps/electron-demo with an absolute-positioned status bar\nin the editor container (CSS at the bottom of style.css).\n\nTests: 45 new vitest cases (34 pure-function + 11 plugin/status-bar\nintegration). Full suite: 362/362 green. pnpm typecheck clean.\npnpm build + pnpm build:electron-demo both succeed.\n\nWorkspace integration: tsconfig.base.json path alias, vitest.config.ts\nresolve alias, root package.json build script, README plugin tables\n(en + zh), ROADMAP rows (en + zh), CONTRIBUTING scope whitelist\n(en + zh).\n\nOpenSpec: openspec/changes/add-plugin-wordcount/ with proposal.md,\ntasks.md (all completed bar two flagged-with-rationale boxes),\ndesign.md (7 decisions + risks + open questions), and a wordcount\ncapability spec delta with 8 requirements / 23 scenarios.\n\nRoadmap entry: #28 under 'Developer Experience'. No breaking changes\nto existing public APIs.",
      "date": "2026-06-17T07:48:34Z"
    }
  ],
